From b8cf2da02d1bbf784370c77dff53c21ecf44c474 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 09:14:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Instagram-style pull-to-refresh
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New reusable engine (public/js/pull-to-refresh.js): touch-only,
  activates only at scrollTop 0, rubber-band pull with rotating
  indicator, threshold-triggered async refresh, duplicate-refresh
  guard, clean destroy().
- Wired into the SPA shell's shared .content container, dispatching
  to the existing loadFromCloud()+renderAll() cycle (same one the
  5s sync loop already uses) for all main pages.
- Separate instance on #chatMsgs calling Chat.loadMessages().
- Iframe-hosted pages (collection.html, globe.html) get their own
  instance on their own document scroll, reusing their existing
  init()/loadMemories() fetch paths.
- Other iframe pages (music/games/movie/lovecounter/dreamgoals/
  meetplanner/places/dailyroutine) intentionally left out of this
  pass — touch input inside an <iframe> never reaches the shell's
  listeners, and wiring per-page refresh there needs the same
  function-mapping care given to collection/globe.
- Shell excludes chat/camera/ai/virtualhome + all iframe pages from
  its own .content instance so it never no-ops or double-fires.
